cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Opod in academic work or a published project, please cite it as below."
title: "Opod: a self-hosted LLM gateway for multi-machine inference clusters"
abstract: |
  Opod is a CLI-only Go binary that turns a fleet of Macs and Linux boxes
  into a private inference cluster behind a single OpenAI-compatible
  endpoint. It ships a per-user API key system with scopes, rpm/tpm and
  daily-token quotas, expiry and an audit log; multi-node routing that
  picks a worker per request by load; sharding of one model across
  machines on three backends (llama.cpp RPC, vLLM + Ray, and SGLang's own
  distributed launcher); and Prometheus metrics with OpenTelemetry traces.
  Nothing leaves the operator's network: there is no vendor egress and no
  telemetry. The runtime is engine-agnostic — Ollama, vLLM, SGLang,
  MLX-LM and llama.cpp drivers ship out of the box.
